cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use the ORCT format, its method or its datasets, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "ORCT: Open Road Charge Tariff"
version: "0.3"
abstract: >-
  ORCT is an open format for road charges (tolls, vignettes, zone and
  congestion charges, external-cost charges and carbon prices on fuel) and a
  normative method to compute the charges of one vehicle's trip from them.
  It encodes the ISO 17575-3 tariff concept model as open JSON, extends it to
  closed entry-exit systems, time-based vignettes and carbon prices on fuel,
  and adds exact money, tax basis, provenance and coverage. The repository
  holds the specification, JSON schemas, conformance tests and datasets for
  about 40 European countries, each sourced from the law or official tariff.
authors:
  - family-names: Ghafouri
    given-names: Majid
repository-code: "https://github.com/majidkabir/orct"
license:
  - MIT
  - CC-BY-4.0
keywords:
  - road charges
  - road tolls
  - tariff data
  - open standard
  - ISO 17575-3
  - Eurovignette
  - carbon pricing
  - ETS2
  - freight transport
